# Exported symbols of libgoldberry -- the complete native surface.
#
# Everything is compiled with hidden visibility and the statically linked
# upstreams are excluded from re-export, so a symbol reaches Java only by being
# listed here. The build turns this file into a linker version script on Linux,
# an -exported_symbols_list on macOS, and a .def on Windows, and forces each
# symbol to be pulled out of its static archive with -u.
#
# This file is the mirror of the Java binding registry: a symbol bound in Java
# but missing here fails at load time with an unresolved-symbol error, and a
# symbol here that nothing binds is dead weight. Keeping the two in step is the
# same discipline ADR-0010 applies to struct layouts.
#
# Blank lines and #-comments are ignored. One symbol per line.
#
# ASCII ONLY, including in comments. CMake's file(STRINGS) extracts runs of
# printable ASCII, so a non-ASCII byte splits the line -- a comment containing
# one returns its tail as a separate element that no longer starts with '#', and
# the parser hands that fragment to the linker as a symbol name. The build now
# rejects anything that is not a valid C identifier, but keeping this file ASCII
# avoids the problem at its source. (Hence "sec. 4" rather than the section sign
# used elsewhere in the docs.)

# --- libgoldberry's own surface ---------------------------------------------
goldberry_abi_version
goldberry_layout_table
goldberry_layout_count

# Calls a YGMeasureFunc upcall stub and reports what the struct-by-value return
# delivered. See sec. 3.1 and ADR-0017.
goldberry_probe_measure

# --- SDL3 (sec. 4, backend SPI) ----------------------------------------------
# Lifecycle, error and version. Enough to prove SDL3 is reachable through this
# list and to report which SDL is linked in; windowing follows.
SDL_Init
SDL_InitSubSystem
SDL_QuitSubSystem
SDL_WasInit
SDL_Quit
SDL_GetError
SDL_ClearError
SDL_GetVersion
SDL_GetRevision

# --- Blend2D (sec. 5, paint & raster) ----------------------------------------

# --- Yoga (sec. 5, layout) ---------------------------------------------------

# --- HarfBuzz (sec. 6, text) -------------------------------------------------

# --- libxkbcommon (Linux/Scarlet only, sec. 7.1) -----------------------------
